{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The fifth time</b><br>They emboldened me. [Stronger than me, or] they removed my Rahab and my dominion from the quarry of Rahab [and their Rahab is toil and iniquity]." "<b>The third time</b><br>Now you will yet be beautiful, and the nations of the world will fear you; therefore your prophets will cease from you — this is [the meaning of] \"turn away your eyes.\" Therefore your nazirites and your men of war will return."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The bracketed text appears to be an alternate gloss; the passage is cryptic and possibly corrupt, translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:43.824244576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}